# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Binary assets, said out loud rather than left to git's NUL-byte heuristic.
#
# Three test files assert that re-running a generator reproduces a committed
# .glb BYTE FOR BYTE (ship-assets, bastion-asset, ship-dray, pike-assets,
# npc-assets). Any line-ending normalisation applied to those bytes on
# checkout would fail every one of them, and it would fail them in a way this
# project has already been bitten by once: `core.autocrlf` has previously made
# a scrape green in a worktree and red in the checkout of the same commit.
#
# The heuristic would almost certainly get these right on its own. "Almost
# certainly" is not what a byte-for-byte assertion should rest on.
*.glb binary
*.ktx2 binary
*.wasm binary
